Report cloud-init completion only once it is seen, and print it once.

The cloud-init watch reported Completed when it ended for any reason: an SSH
stream that ended early (sshd restarting during provisioning, a dropped
connection) or a final read without the completion line counted as success,
so limactl start took a first boot as provisioned while cloud-init still ran.
The watch now reopens the log stream, with backoff, until it sees cloud-init
finish or its context ends; lines a reopened stream replays are not reported
again. Its last event claims completion only if cloud-init finished.

Every hostagent event repeats the last cloud-init progress, so limactl start
printed the same cloud-init line, and "progress monitoring done.", with each
port forwarding or vsock event. It now prints progress only when it changes.

